# Functorial Species → Tropical Valuation Profiles via Exponential Generating Functions

Bridge: connects **combinatorial species / EGFs** (`Applications/CombinatorialSpecies.lean`)
to **tropical (min-plus) valuation data** (`Bridges/CategoricalTropicalUltrametric.lean`,
`Computation/PadicValuationDepth.lean`).

## Mathematical theme

A combinatorial species `F` has a counting sequence `aₙ = |F[n]|`.  Its exponential
generating function is `egf a = ∑ₙ (aₙ/n!) Xⁿ`, and the *structural (Day-convolution)
product* of species corresponds (by `CombinatorialSpecies.card_prodSpecies`,
`CombinatorialSpecies.egf_mul`) to the **binomial convolution**

  `(a ⋆ b)ₙ = ∑_{i+j=n} C(n,i) aᵢ bⱼ`

of counting sequences, which the EGF turns into the *ordinary product* of power series.

The new object of this file is the **tropical valuation profile** of a counting sequence
relative to a prime `p`:

  `valProfile p a n = emultiplicity p (aₙ) ∈ ℕ∞`,

i.e. the `p`-adic valuation of the `n`-th term, valued in the tropical semiring
`(ℕ∞, min, +)`.  We use `emultiplicity` rather than `padicValNat` precisely so the value at
`0` is `⊤`, the tropical additive unit — this is what makes the ultrametric/min-plus
inequalities below hold with *no* positivity side conditions.

The central message: **the species product is a lax (min-plus) monoidal functor into the
tropical semiring**.  Concretely, the valuation profile of a binomial convolution is bounded
*below*, in the tropical sense, by the min-plus convolution of the two profiles:

  `min_{i+j=n} (valProfile p a i + valProfile p b j)  ≤  valProfile p (a ⋆ b) n`.

This is the tropical shadow of the analytic product law `egf (a⋆b) = egf a · egf b`: where
the EGF turns the species product into the *ordinary* product of power series, the valuation
profile turns it into the *tropical* (min-plus) product of profiles — but only as a one-sided
lower bound, since the binomial coefficients and additive cancellation can only raise the
valuation.

This file is intentionally self-contained (`import Mathlib` only): it re-derives the small
cardinality fact it needs (`card_daySumProduct`, the type-family core of
`CombinatorialSpecies.card_prodSpecies`) so that it does not depend on the exact build wiring
of the species file, while connecting to it conceptually.

## Main results
* `valProfile`                        — the tropical valuation profile of a counting sequence.
* `binConvNat`                        — the `ℕ`-valued binomial convolution (species product).
* `finset_inf_emultiplicity_le_sum`   — ultrametric: `inf` of valuations `≤` valuation of a sum.
* `tropical_sum_law`                  — `min` law: profile of a sum dominates the `min` profile.
* `tropical_product_lower_bound`      — min-plus convolution lower-bounds the product profile.
* `card_daySumProduct`                — cardinality of the Day-convolution = binomial convolution.
* `tropical_product_lower_bound_card` — the functorial (structure-level) statement.
* `padicValRat_egfCoeff`              — EGF coefficient valuation = profile − factorial profile.
-/
import Mathlib

open scoped BigOperators
open Finset

namespace SpeciesTropicalValuationProfiles

noncomputable section

/-! ### The tropical valuation profile -/

/-- The **tropical valuation profile** of a counting sequence `a : ℕ → ℕ` at a prime `p`:
the `p`-adic valuation `emultiplicity p (aₙ)` of the `n`-th term, valued in `ℕ∞`.  The value
at a vanishing term is `⊤`, the additive unit of the tropical semiring `(ℕ∞, min, +)`. -/
def valProfile (p : ℕ) (a : ℕ → ℕ) (n : ℕ) : ℕ∞ := emultiplicity p (a n)

@[simp] lemma valProfile_def (p : ℕ) (a : ℕ → ℕ) (n : ℕ) :
    valProfile p a n = emultiplicity p (a n) := rfl

/-- The `ℕ`-valued **binomial convolution** of two counting sequences, i.e. the counting
sequence of the structural (Day-convolution) product of the corresponding species. -/
def binConvNat (a b : ℕ → ℕ) (n : ℕ) : ℕ :=
  ∑ q ∈ Finset.antidiagonal n, n.choose q.1 * a q.1 * b q.2

/-! ### The ultrametric (tropical) inequalities -/

-- !-- Lab Notes -- !--
-- Hypothesis: the binomial convolution (= species product) should descend to a *min-plus*
--   (tropical) lower bound on `p`-adic valuation profiles, mirroring how the EGF turns the
--   species product into the ordinary product of power series (`egf_mul`).
-- The backbone is the classic ultrametric `min(v a, v b) ≤ v(a+b)` (`min_le_emultiplicity_add`)
--   promoted to finite sums (`finset_inf_emultiplicity_le_sum`), combined with the additivity
--   of valuation over products (`emultiplicity_mul`, valid since `ℕ` is a cancellative
--   `CommMonoidWithZero`).  Working in `ℕ∞` (not `ℕ`) is essential: it sends a vanishing term
--   to `⊤`, the tropical additive unit, so no positivity hypotheses are needed.
-- Outcome: all four core inequalities proved with no positivity hypotheses, confirming the
--   "species product is a lax min-plus functor" hypothesis. The lower bound is genuinely
--   one-sided: e.g. `C(2,1) = 2` injects a factor of `2`, so for `p = 2` the convolution
--   valuation strictly exceeds the min-plus convolution — the binomial coefficients break
--   exactness, which is why we get an inequality (lax functor), not an identity.

/-- **Ultrametric for finite sums.** The `p`-adic valuation of a finite sum is at least the
infimum (tropical sum) of the valuations of the summands. -/
lemma finset_inf_emultiplicity_le_sum {ι : Type*} (p : ℕ) (s : Finset ι) (f : ι → ℕ) :
    (s.inf fun i => emultiplicity p (f i)) ≤ emultiplicity p (∑ i ∈ s, f i) := by
  classical
  induction s using Finset.induction with
  | empty => simp
  | insert a s ha ih =>
      rw [Finset.inf_insert, Finset.sum_insert ha]
      refine le_trans ?_ (min_le_emultiplicity_add (p := p) (a := f a) (b := ∑ i ∈ s, f i))
      exact le_min inf_le_left (le_trans inf_le_right ih)

/-- **Tropical sum law.** The valuation profile of a pointwise sum of counting sequences
dominates the `min` (tropical sum) of the two profiles — the analytic shadow of `egf_add`
on the valuation side. -/
theorem tropical_sum_law (p : ℕ) (a b : ℕ → ℕ) (n : ℕ) :
    min (valProfile p a n) (valProfile p b n) ≤ valProfile p (fun m => a m + b m) n := by
  simpa using min_le_emultiplicity_add (p := p) (a := a n) (b := b n)

/-- Each term of the binomial convolution has valuation at least the sum of the input
valuations, since the binomial coefficient contributes a non-negative amount. -/
lemma valProfile_add_le_term (p : ℕ) (hp : Prime p) (a b : ℕ → ℕ) (n : ℕ) (q : ℕ × ℕ) :
    valProfile p a q.1 + valProfile p b q.2
      ≤ emultiplicity p (n.choose q.1 * a q.1 * b q.2) := by
  rw [emultiplicity_mul hp, emultiplicity_mul hp, valProfile_def, valProfile_def]
  gcongr
  exact le_add_self

/-- **Tropical product lower bound (the bridge).** The valuation profile of the species
product `a ⋆ b` is bounded below, in the tropical semiring `(ℕ∞, min, +)`, by the *min-plus
convolution* of the profiles of `a` and `b`:

  `min_{i+j=n} (valProfile p a i + valProfile p b j) ≤ valProfile p (a ⋆ b) n`.

This is the tropical shadow of the analytic product law `egf (a⋆b) = egf a · egf b`. -/
theorem tropical_product_lower_bound (p : ℕ) (hp : Prime p) (a b : ℕ → ℕ) (n : ℕ) :
    (Finset.antidiagonal n).inf (fun q => valProfile p a q.1 + valProfile p b q.2)
      ≤ valProfile p (binConvNat a b) n := by
  refine le_trans (Finset.inf_mono_fun ?_)
    (finset_inf_emultiplicity_le_sum p (Finset.antidiagonal n)
      (fun q => n.choose q.1 * a q.1 * b q.2))
  intro q _
  exact valProfile_add_le_term p hp a b n q

/-! ### The functorial (structure-level) statement -/

-- !-- Lab Notes -- !--
-- `card_daySumProduct` is the type-family core of `CombinatorialSpecies.card_prodSpecies`:
--   the Day-convolution structure set `Σ S ⊆ [n], A[|S|] × B[n∖S]` has cardinality the
--   binomial convolution of the counting sequences `|A[·]|`, `|B[·]|`. We reprove it so the
--   tropical bound applies directly to *structures*, not just abstract sequences. The proof
--   groups subsets `S ⊆ [n]` by their cardinality `k` (there are `C(n,k)` of them), exactly
--   as in the species file. This makes `tropical_product_lower_bound_card` a statement about
--   the relabelling-functorial Day product, i.e. genuinely functorial species data.

/-- **Cardinality of the Day-convolution product** (the type-family core of
`CombinatorialSpecies.card_prodSpecies`): the structure set `Σ S ⊆ [n], A[|S|] × B[n∖S]` has
cardinality the binomial convolution of the cards. -/
theorem card_daySumProduct (A B : ℕ → Type) [∀ k, Fintype (A k)] [∀ k, Fintype (B k)] (n : ℕ) :
    Fintype.card (Σ S : Finset (Fin n), A S.card × B (n - S.card))
      = binConvNat (fun k => Fintype.card (A k)) (fun k => Fintype.card (B k)) n := by
  simp +decide only [Fintype.card_sigma, Fintype.card_prod, binConvNat]
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun x _ => by rw [mul_comm]]
  rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun x _ => by rw [mul_comm]]
  rw [Finset.Nat.sum_antidiagonal_eq_sum_range_succ_mk]
  rw [show (Finset.univ : Finset (Finset (Fin n)))
        = Finset.biUnion (Finset.range (n + 1))
            fun k => Finset.powersetCard k (Finset.univ : Finset (Fin n)) from ?_,
      Finset.sum_biUnion]
  · refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
    rw [Finset.sum_congr rfl fun j hj => by rw [Finset.mem_powersetCard.mp hj |>.2]]
    simp +decide [mul_assoc]
  · exact fun i _ j _ hij => Finset.disjoint_left.mpr fun x hx₁ hx₂ =>
      hij <| by rw [Finset.mem_powersetCard] at hx₁ hx₂; aesop
  · ext s
    simp [Finset.mem_biUnion, Finset.mem_powersetCard]
    exact le_trans (Finset.card_le_univ _) (by norm_num)

/-- **Functorial species → tropical bridge.** For finite structure families `A`, `B`, the
valuation profile of the structural (Day-convolution) product is tropically lower-bounded by
the min-plus convolution of the profiles of `A` and `B`.  This combines `card_daySumProduct`
(cardinality = binomial convolution) with `tropical_product_lower_bound`. -/
theorem tropical_product_lower_bound_card (p : ℕ) (hp : Prime p)
    (A B : ℕ → Type) [∀ k, Fintype (A k)] [∀ k, Fintype (B k)] (n : ℕ) :
    (Finset.antidiagonal n).inf
        (fun q => emultiplicity p (Fintype.card (A q.1)) + emultiplicity p (Fintype.card (B q.2)))
      ≤ emultiplicity p
          (Fintype.card (Σ S : Finset (Fin n), A S.card × B (n - S.card))) := by
  have h := tropical_product_lower_bound p hp
    (fun k => Fintype.card (A k)) (fun k => Fintype.card (B k)) n
  rw [card_daySumProduct]
  simpa [valProfile] using h

/-! ### The exponential generating function viewpoint -/

-- !-- Lab Notes -- !--
-- The EGF coefficient `coeff n (egf a) = aₙ / n!` ties the valuation profile to the EGF: its
--   `p`-adic valuation is the profile *shifted by the factorial valuation profile*
--   `n ↦ padicValNat p n!` (the Legendre / de Polignac sequence). So the EGF transform
--   subtracts the (purely arithmetic) factorial profile from the (combinatorial) species
--   profile. This is the precise sense in which the tropical profile travels "via the EGF":
--   `valProfile_EGF n = valProfile_species n − factorialProfile n`. Since the factorial
--   profile is independent of the species, the EGF preserves *relative* valuation data and
--   only retunes the absolute baseline.

/-- **EGF coefficient valuation.** The `p`-adic valuation of the `n`-th EGF coefficient
`aₙ / n!` of a counting sequence equals its valuation profile minus the *factorial valuation
profile* `padicValNat p n!`.  Thus the EGF subtracts the factorial (Legendre) profile from
the species valuation profile. -/
theorem padicValRat_egfCoeff (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (a : ℕ → ℕ) (n : ℕ) (h : a n ≠ 0) :
    padicValRat p ((a n : ℚ) / (n.factorial : ℚ))
      = (padicValNat p (a n) : ℤ) - (padicValNat p n.factorial : ℤ) := by
  rw [padicValRat.div] <;> simp [h, Nat.factorial_ne_zero]

end

end SpeciesTropicalValuationProfiles
